        "procedure": "A suspension of Tb(ClO4)3·6H2O (0.2 mmol, 0.1131 g) and H2L (0.2 mmol, 0.0575 g) in CH3OH–CH3COCH3 (10 mL–10 mL) was treated with NaOH (0.4 mmol, 0.016 g). The resultant orange solution was stirred for 6 h and subsequently filtered. The filtrate was left undisturbed for slow solvent evaporation. Orange plate-shaped single crystals of 1 suitable for X-ray diffraction formed after one week.",
