      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Prepared as for 1, substituting Dy(ClO4)3·6H2O (0.2 mmol, 0.1138 g) for Tb(ClO4)3·6H2O. Thus Dy(ClO4)3·6H2O and H2L (0.2 mmol, 0.0575 g) in CH3OH–CH3COCH3 (10 mL–10 mL) were treated with NaOH (0.4 mmol, 0.016 g), stirred 6 h, filtered, and crystallized by slow evaporation over one week.",
