      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "The Y-shaped Dy4 cluster is the only analogue showing SMM-like slow relaxation. χT is 52.60 cm3 K mol−1 at 300 K and 27.73 cm3 K mol−1 at 1.9 K; magnetization reaches 20.62 μB at 1.9 K and 7 T with a dM/dH kink near 4000 Oe indicating antiferromagnetic Dy–Dy coupling. Zero-field ac data show temperature- and frequency-dependent χ″ below ~22 K with dual Orbach barriers Ueff = 7.6(1) K (τ0 = 5.2(1)×10−3 s) and 83.7(3) K (τ0 = 9.5(3)×10−8 s); Cole–Cole α = 0.24–0.33 (13–K range). Applied fields of 100–1000 Oe at 1.9 K barely change the ac profile.",
        "measurements": [
          {
            "property_type": "magnetic",
            "name": "χT",
            "value": "52.60",
            "unit": "cm3 K mol−1",
            "conditions": "300 K; 1000 Oe"
          },
          {
            "property_type": "magnetic",
            "name": "χT",
            "value": "27.73",
            "unit": "cm3 K mol−1",
            "conditions": "1.9 K"
